Z||000003||Shiner||03-18-2000||12:17 AM||||Doughboy,<P> My buddy uses his older Sony CarDiscman in his Saab 900 all the time.  He uses one of those adapters with the cassete at the end.  If you have a decent tape deck, it really doesn't sound bad at all.  It really doesn't skip much, unless he hits a pretty good sized pot hole, and his suspension is pretty stiff (I think he has Bilstiens on there now!)  I guess the skip-factor will all depend on what kind of discman you are using.  My old discman which was not designed for car use is pretty much un-listenable unless you are cruising on a very smooth highway.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||kupop87gt||03-18-2000||12:40 AM||||I bought a Sony Discman this last fall for other uses and decided to try it out. It works quite well; the sound quality isn't noticably poor. As for skipping, this unit has NEVER skipped, and we're talking about an '87 GT on snow-battered Wisconsin roads.<BR>A friend of mine has a Civic with either an aftermarket or dealer cd adapter through the radio. It actually worked fine. I was suprised.||||reg||1
